{
  "spike": "S0.8 — AoI cell-grid micro-benchmark (cell grid per ARCHITECTURE.md §6; rebuild-subscriptions-per-tick semantics; benchmark doubles as the algorithm spec for the Phase-5 Go port)",
  "date": "2026-09-06",
  "host": "Windows 11 dev box (Ryzen 7 7445HS, RTX 4050 Laptop, 15.2 GB RAM), Node single process",
  "toolVersions": {
    "node": "v24.13.0",
    "typescript": "7.0.2 (dev tooling, caret-pinned; spike files are excluded from the repo typecheck program per CLAUDE.md carve-out)",
    "vitest": "5.0.0 (dev tooling, caret-pinned)"
  },
  "repro": "node tools/spikes/s0.8/bench.mjs — placement and movement RNG fully seeded (mulberry32, per-config derived seed); timing rows vary run to run by their nature. Correctness of the algorithm under test: npx vitest run tools/spikes/s0.8",
  "method": {
    "grid": "tools/spikes/s0.8/aoi.ts is both the benchmark implementation and the normative algorithm spec for the Phase-5 Go port (ARCHITECTURE.md §6: \"per tick, the runtime computes each client's area of interest as a set of cells (own cell + radius)\"; NETWORKING.md §5/§9). Static square grid, cell = (floor(x/cs), floor(z/cs)); membership = one long-lived member array per cell, swap-remove is O(cell population), emptied cells pruned; per tick, REBUILD semantics (no incremental diff): every presence is an observer, its AoI is the set of cells whose closed rectangle intersects the 500 m disc around it (nearest-point/clamp test, f64), candidate cell range padded one ring beyond the raw floor bounds so exact tangency and f64 rounding survive (the rect test is the authority); interest set = member ids of those cells minus the observer; interest buffers reused across ticks so a rebuild tick allocates nothing.",
    "bench": "perf_hooks performance.now() around two per-tick phases: (1) move phase — every presence takes one random-direction step of 0.07 m (1.4 m/s walk at the assumed 20 Hz tick rate) with reflection at the 5x5 km boundary, applied through grid.move(); the span includes one mulberry32 call per presence, which bounds the AoI-independent floor of the tick cost; (2) rebuild phase — one grid.rebuildTick() rebuilding every presence's interest set from scratch. Headline \"full rebuild tick\" = move + rebuild spans together (mean/p50/p99/max over 300 measured ticks after 30 warmup ticks; p99 is the 297th of 300 sorted samples, nearest-rank). Per-tick stats passes (max cell population, interest-set sizes) run OUTSIDE the timed spans. Configs run sequentially in one process; GC pauses inside the measured window are included by design — managed-runtime honesty, and one reason the Node numbers are not Go numbers.",
    "distributions": {
      "uniform": "x,z ~ U(0, 5000) independently over the 5x5 km area (density N / 25e6 m^2).",
      "clustered": "Stone-Town-like dense centre: 80% of presences uniform in the centred square of side sqrt(0.10)*5000 = 1581.1388 m (area 2.5e6 m^2 = 10% of the area), remaining 20% uniform over the full area; expected hotspot density 0.8N / 2.5e6 m^2."
    },
    "interestMetrics": "maxCellPopulation = max over the 300 measured ticks of the largest cell member array (per-tick scan outside the timed spans); finalCellPopulationP50/P90/Max = nearest-rank percentiles of the cell-population snapshot at the final tick; maxInterestPopulation = max over measured ticks of any single observer's rebuilt interest set (the driver of the coalesced per-presence broadcast size); meanInterestPopulation = mean per observer; meanAoiCellCount = mean size of the AoI CELL set over a <=500-presence sample at the final tick (geometry of the rect-intersect-disc rule).",
    "messageSize": "DERIVATION, clearly not a measurement: the measured populations are combined with the NETWORKING.md §4 hard cap (<=1500 B per message, ~1 message per tick per presence — the coalesced per-presence broadcast framing) and a STATED wire model (field ledger below) that the Phase-5 netcode design doc must replace with its own byte ledger. A per-cell broadcast framing is noted for contrast: it would emit meanAoiCellCount messages per presence per tick, violating the one-message rule outright."
  },
